Prices shown do not include VAT, which is added at 5%.

== What this means for you

The unit price is what you pay for each kWh of electricity you use. From 1 October 2026 it rises by £0.05, from £0.29 to £0.34 per kWh. The standing charge is a fixed daily amount you pay whatever you use. It stays at £0.48 per day.

A home that uses 210 kWh a month would pay about £10.50 more each month before VAT.

== Estimated readings

When we cannot read your meter, we estimate your reading from your usage in the same month last year. An estimate can be higher or lower than what you really used. If you send us an actual reading, we will replace the estimate and send you a corrected bill.

== Leaving this tariff

You can switch tariff or supplier at any time. There is no exit fee on Home Standard.
